1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,900
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:10,570
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:14,540
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,520
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:21,480
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,460
H-Hey!

7
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,140
Guts!

8
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:06,500
Feel no shame about shape

9
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,420
Weather changes their phrase

10
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:12,170
Even mother will show you another way

11
00:01:12,170 --> 00:01:14,550
So put your glasses on

12
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:16,630
Nothing will be wrong

13
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

14
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,680
It's up to you

15
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:24,310
The first words should be found

16
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:27,940
Whatever holds you back

17
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:29,310
I...

18
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:30,440
...can...

19
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:32,610
I can get it off

20
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:33,610
Tell me what...

21
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:34,610
Tell me what...

22
00:01:34,610 --> 00:01:36,450
Tell me what you want

23
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:37,530
I don't know why...

24
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:38,530
Don't know why...

25
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,530
Don't know why you're afraid

26
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,700
Tell me what...

27
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:42,660
Tell me what...

28
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:44,330
Tell me what you'd say

29
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:45,660
I don't know why...

30
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:46,750
Don't know why...

31
00:01:46,830 --> 00:01:47,540
Too late...

32
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,170
It's too late

33
00:01:54,090 --> 00:01:58,090
Together

34
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:02,220
It's up to you whether to follow me or not.

35
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:07,350
You've learned what it means to fight, haven't you?

36
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:29,790
Hey.

37
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:41,220
Where am I?

38
00:02:41,550 --> 00:02:43,550
You are in a cave by the river.

39
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:45,720
Luckily, we fell into the river and survived.

40
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,640
A river?

41
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:51,100
Come on, don't you remember anything?

42
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:55,190
Funny you can be so nonchalant.
We nearly drowned to death!

43
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:58,990
Damn it!

44
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:01,530
Don't get up yet. Your fever
hasn't completely gone down.

45
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:10,160
You can't blame me. You were
freezing and completely drenched.

46
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,210
What are you looking at?

47
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:20,050
That hurt!
What's the meaning of this?

48
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,340
I'm the one who saved your life!

49
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,180
Shit, stop it!

50
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:26,890
Oh, lay off!

51
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,280
Enough of this crap!

52
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,610
You're hysterical!

53
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:43,110
I don't want to make a big deal out of it...

54
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:46,490
But I risked my life dragging you out
of that river in your damned armor!

55
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:48,660
You could show a little gratitude, at least!

56
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,120
But instead you hurl a knife at me?

57
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:54,120
I'd beat you and dislocate
your jaw if you weren't a woman!

58
00:03:56,380 --> 00:04:00,710
I do not like it, a mere woman
such as you acting like a knight.

59
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:04,550
You're easily driven into a frenzy.

60
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,930
That's why a woman like you isn't cut out for war.

61
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:11,560
Hey...

62
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,150
Not my choice...

63
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,820
I was not...

64
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:24,280
I was not born as a woman by choice!

65
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,780
Well, I'm sorry.

66
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:32,330
Damn you!

67
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:34,120
You crazy broad!

68
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,540
Why don't you try to calm down?

69
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,830
Hands off!

70
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:39,000
Let go...

71
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,380
...of me...

72
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:48,930
I told you so.

73
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:53,890
Hey, put this on.

74
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,650
It dried out while I was wearing it.

75
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:00,520
What?

76
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,730
Are you still crying?

77
00:05:02,110 --> 00:05:02,900
Shut up!

78
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:03,820
Turn around now!

79
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,570
How pathetic...

80
00:05:07,570 --> 00:05:10,580
You are the last person
I would ever want to be rescued by!

81
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,950
Great, she really hates me.

82
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:19,080
Hey, why did you enlist in
the Band of the Hawk anyway?

83
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:21,750
Isn't it tough to be a woman in this business?

84
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:23,550
No matter the circumstances...

85
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,470
Well, it's not my business, I guess.

86
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,510
Griffith...

87
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,440
It's because of Griffith.

88
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:46,650
I'm from a small farming
village deep in the mountains.

89
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:52,080
The crops were meager,
and the soil was sterile...

90
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:58,670
Nevertheless, we had been bled
dry by heavy taxes for the war effort.

91
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:03,500
Frequently, we would eat
nothing for three days at a time.

92
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:08,800
Many people died of hunger each winter...

93
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:13,850
Our village was along the border,
so it often was involved in skirmishes.

94
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:17,270
Each time it happened...

95
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:21,610
We were forced to quietly watch
our houses and fields be trampled.

96
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:24,940
There were similar stories
from all the nearby villages.

97
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:29,950
Everyone was used to being looted
and having their lives crushed...

98
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:34,160
And I thought it was
just a matter of course.

99
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,660
One day...

100
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:45,130
A nobleman was passing by our village...

101
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,760
...and I caught his eye.

102
00:06:48,970 --> 00:06:53,100
The nobleman offered
to take me as his waiting maid.

103
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:57,720
After hesitating for a while, my father
ended up accepting his offer.

104
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:02,650
I knew why my father would give
his youngest daughter to the noble...

105
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:04,730
I was not much help to the family.

106
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:07,190
My parents had to reduce
the number of mouths to feed.

107
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:08,940
However...

108
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,340
It's no wonder that
it turned out the way it did...

109
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:32,130
It couldn't be true...

110
00:07:32,130 --> 00:07:34,010
...that a noble would, on a whim...

111
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:37,470
...save the daughter of some
poor man purely out of kindness.

112
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:49,860
There's nothing I can do...

113
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,860
This is just how things are...

114
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:57,450
Those were the only thoughts
that kept me chained to reality.

115
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:10,550
Just because you were born a noble,
do you believe you're chosen by God?

116
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:16,350
He looked divine, and the moment was unreal.

117
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:22,480
God mercifully sent an angel
to this pathetic, powerless girl.

118
00:08:23,230 --> 00:08:25,850
I really believed that for a moment.

119
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:32,650
But what the angel gave me
was not the helping hand I expected.

120
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:37,740
If there is something you wish
to protect, take up that sword!

121
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,270
I was frightened.

122
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:06,850
Did I stab him with the sword...

123
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:10,650
...or did he accidentally impale himself?

124
00:09:12,030 --> 00:09:15,570
Either way, I had killed a man.

125
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:28,580
The stranger just nodded slowly and knowingly.

126
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:36,050
It was then I realized that he had
extended to me a true helping hand.

127
00:09:37,010 --> 00:09:39,470
Griffith, we've cleared everything out.

128
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,890
Hey, wait...

129
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,350
What am I supposed to do?

130
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:53,820
Do whatever you like.

131
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:57,150
I want...

132
00:09:59,110 --> 00:10:00,820
Please bring me with you!

133
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:04,160
No way, don't be silly.

134
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,710
We are not just petty thieves!

135
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:10,290
We are collecting war funds
in order to raise an army!

136
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:13,630
It'd be a joke if we went off to war
accompanied by kids and women!

137
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:17,760
Please, I will learn how to wield
a sword if that's what it takes!

138
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:18,680
So please...

139
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:21,260
Oh boy, she's serious.

140
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,510
What if you wind up dead?

141
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,350
I told you...

142
00:10:29,690 --> 00:10:31,360
Do whatever you like.

143
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,020
It's up to you whether to follow me or not.

144
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:37,360
You've learned what it means to fight, haven't you?

145
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,080
Yes, but...

146
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:48,870
It's because this sword and blanket
were given to me from you.

147
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:53,920
Everything has changed since the day I met him.

148
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,420
From a life of enduring
and waiting for things to happen...

149
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,420
...to a life where I would
fight for my aspirations.

150
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:04,180
Of course, I worshiped Griffith.

151
00:11:10,850 --> 00:11:11,850
I think...

152
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:15,860
...I'm still lost in a dream.

153
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:21,410
A group of outcasts and commoners
became invincible on the battlefield.

154
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,910
It's like a miracle
the way we have fought.

155
00:11:26,490 --> 00:11:32,080
Above everything, our leader is
a youth, seemingly still so innocent.

156
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:35,880
His origin is even common, just like ours.

157
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:37,920
A miracle!

158
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:42,300
For me, Griffith is the embodiment of a miracle!

159
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:49,220
While I somehow managed to thrive as a soldier...

160
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:54,310
...we became involved in a territorial
dispute led by a local nobleman.

161
00:11:55,650 --> 00:12:00,400
The nobleman was
well-known and very wealthy.

162
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:04,990
But he had a bad reputation
that didn't reflect his wealth...

163
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:06,870
...but rather his unsavory tastes.

164
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:12,500
Officially, he hired young kids
from villages as his valets.

165
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:17,250
In reality, they were imprisoned
to serve his taste for pederasty.

166
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,630
Their eyes looked vacant
and numbly frightened.

167
00:12:24,550 --> 00:12:27,680
I felt a chill go down my spine.

168
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:32,230
Fear and hatred welled up inside me.
I was totally horrified at the sight.

169
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:36,150
It reminded me that such
a thing could have happened to me.

170
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,070
It was the same hand that saved me...

171
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:44,780
...that he put on my shoulder then.

172
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,910
Somehow, that was all
he had to do to stop my shivering.

173
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,370
Later, after we had been
through several skirmishes...

174
00:12:55,620 --> 00:13:01,380
The boy was an apprentice soldier
who had joined us half a year before.

175
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,470
Griffith.

176
00:13:05,090 --> 00:13:06,220
What's that?

177
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,840
The boy's belongings...

178
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,600
Griffith?

179
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:18,650
He must have really wanted to be a knight.

180
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:25,150
I remember this boy well.

181
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:31,080
He always gazed at me as one
might admire the hero of a story.

182
00:13:34,410 --> 00:13:36,830
I wonder if he was happy.

183
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:41,420
Did he die as if in a dream,
one close to being fulfilled?

184
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:47,680
I think my dream must have murdered this boy.

185
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:54,720
Before then, I had never
seen Griffith so depressed.

186
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,850
A man like Griffith let his shoulders droop.

187
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:03,940
And since that moment, Griffith
gradually began to look different.

188
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:08,150
A few nights after our return from that battle...

189
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:17,000
Griffith!

190
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:27,220
No way, you've got to be kidding!

191
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:29,220
A proud guy like him was...

192
00:14:49,610 --> 00:14:50,410
Casca...

193
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,160
It feels so nice. Won't you join me?

194
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:56,910
Well, I, uh...

195
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,120
You think I'm disgusting?

196
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,040
No...

197
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:05,300
Why...

198
00:15:07,210 --> 00:15:09,170
Why were you there last night?

199
00:15:12,550 --> 00:15:16,180
Wait a minute. I was mistaken, right?

200
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:19,810
Last night... you were there
for a war council or something...

201
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:20,890
No...

202
00:15:21,270 --> 00:15:21,980
What?

203
00:15:24,610 --> 00:15:25,690
You weren't mistaken.

204
00:15:28,110 --> 00:15:29,570
How could you? With a man like that?

205
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:32,070
For money.

206
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:36,490
To maintain an army costs lots of money.

207
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:42,000
Soldiers, horses, equipment,
provisions. Nothing is free.

208
00:15:42,870 --> 00:15:46,210
Moreover, the Band of the Hawk
will continue to expand...

209
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,510
And I must lead my army to prosperity.

210
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:52,430
That's why I need such immense war funds.

211
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:59,810
That old man is interested in me,
while I am interested in his fortune...

212
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,850
Our interests have come
to an agreement. That's all.

213
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:05,060
No... even so. No way...

214
00:16:05,650 --> 00:16:07,440
Why can't things stay as they are?

215
00:16:07,770 --> 00:16:11,570
If can keep on winning, we could earn
all the money you need eventually.

216
00:16:11,570 --> 00:16:13,780
That would take a tremendous
amount of time, and...

217
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:19,240
The more we fight in battles,
the more we lose soldiers.

218
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:24,580
You mean like that boy, don't you?

219
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:26,130
No, I don't.

220
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:28,920
I came to this conclusion rationally.

221
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:34,630
Which brings less risk, losing
hundreds of soldiers in ten battles...

222
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:36,510
...or snaring a rich, old man?

223
00:16:37,390 --> 00:16:39,010
Listen, Casca.

224
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:44,770
I feel no responsibility to comrades
who've lost lives under my command.

225
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:51,030
Because they chose to fight in each battle...

226
00:16:52,110 --> 00:16:53,280
Griffith?

227
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,240
Just as I chose this...

228
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,790
But if there is something that...

229
00:17:01,490 --> 00:17:03,040
...I can do for them...

230
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:06,500
Something I can do for the dead...

231
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,250
Then it is to win!

232
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:14,300
I must keep winning to attain my
dream, the same one they clung to...

233
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,720
...and risked their lives for!

234
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:17,510
Griffith, stop it!

235
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:22,560
To realize my dream,
I will perch on top of their corpses.

236
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:24,180
It is a blood-smeared dream, after all.

237
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,150
I don't regret or feel guilty about it.

238
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:34,490
But to risk thousands of lives
while never getting myself dirty...

239
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:38,820
It's not a dream that can be so easily realized!

240
00:17:42,490 --> 00:17:43,620
Stop it.

241
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,580
Don't talk like that anymore.

242
00:17:56,970 --> 00:17:57,680
It's all right.

243
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,100
It's nothing.

244
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:06,310
Griffith had already recovered by the
time he put his hand on my shoulder.

245
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:09,980
And it made me very sad.

246
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,860
Most people have abandoned
their dreams long ago...

247
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:18,030
...but Griffith is still trying to realize his.

248
00:18:18,490 --> 00:18:20,990
But because the dream he chose...

249
00:18:20,990 --> 00:18:23,410
...is so pure and monumental in scale...

250
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:25,370
...the burden he has to carry
is unimaginably heavy.

251
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:32,790
One who plans to achieve great things
inevitably endures terrible things.

252
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,670
He is not innately strong.

253
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:38,420
But now he has to be stronger than ever.

254
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:46,720
I want to stand by him.

255
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:51,100
If he dedicates himself entirely to his dream...

256
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:55,320
If he has to fight to create his dream...

257
00:18:56,400 --> 00:19:00,110
I want to be a sword for him.

258
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:02,820
I want to stand by him.

259
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:07,080
I want to be something important
that will help him fulfill his dream.

260
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:10,080
Once, I believed that my wish would be granted.

261
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:19,510
But then came the time
when you appeared before us.

262
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:30,640
Do you remember what Griffith
said to you on the hill that day?

263
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:34,440
I want you to join us, Guts!

264
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,360
Those words...

265
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:39,400
He had never said such kind words to anyone.

266
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:44,120
I was very irritated by it.

267
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:48,080
You made him say that
about you without any effort at all...

268
00:19:48,490 --> 00:19:49,790
...and I was very envious.

269
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:54,710
I tried to convince myself...

270
00:19:54,710 --> 00:19:59,050
...Griffith only needed you as a soldier,
one who would strengthen us.

271
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:06,550
But a man like Griffith acts impulsively
when something happens to you.

272
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:07,560
It is as if...

273
00:20:07,970 --> 00:20:08,850
As if...

274
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:15,690
Griffith has faith in you...
and yet you...

275
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:18,320
You never think about the consequences!

276
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:27,370
What I can't forgive is how your
selfishness nearly got Griffith killed!

277
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:31,250
I don't care if you drop dead
somewhere in battle!

278
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:36,580
But I'll never forgive you if you ruin the
Band of the Hawk, Griffith's dream!

279
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:42,420
And I can't forgive you for
making Griffith change like he has...

280
00:20:47,510 --> 00:20:48,470
Why?

281
00:20:50,010 --> 00:20:52,640
Why did he choose you?

282
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:54,440
Why you?

283
00:20:58,690 --> 00:21:00,020
W-What are you doing?

284
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:00,570
Shush!

285
00:21:04,650 --> 00:21:07,700
Hey, listen, I think
they're probably dead by now.

286
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,580
Think about how they fell from the cliff...

287
00:21:09,950 --> 00:21:13,290
It doesn't matter whether
they are alive or not.

288
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:17,250
Sir Adon promised us the reward nevertheless...

289
00:21:18,330 --> 00:21:22,710
Because it's their raider leader
and that female commander.

290
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:25,380
Why don't we look around
downstream from here?

291
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:28,470
The bodies may have drifted
because of the current.

292
00:21:32,810 --> 00:21:33,430
Listen.

293
00:21:34,980 --> 00:21:36,560
Take this medicine to lower your fever.

294
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,230
We have no time to rest anymore.

295
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:41,110
We're going as soon as it gets dark.

296
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

297
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

298
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

299
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

300
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

301
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

302
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

303
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

304
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

305
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

306
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

